---
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import { withBase } from "astro-theme-university/url";
import BasketOptimiser from "../../components/BasketOptimiser.astro";
import IndexCalculator from "../../components/IndexCalculator.astro";
import TaxComparator from "../../components/TaxComparator.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../../site-config";
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Toolkit"
  description="Three instruments the course builds and uses: the index calculation, the two tax structures, and the constrained selection."
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <p>
    Everything below is arithmetic you will do by hand in the labs before you
    do it at scale. The tools are here so you can check a single row against
    your own working — a disagreement between your spreadsheet and this page
    is worth finding in week 9 rather than in a submitted portfolio.
  </p>
  <p>
    They are ordered the way the semester is: the unit first, then what
    distorts it, then what to do about it under a constraint.
  </p>

  <IndexCalculator />
  <TaxComparator />
  <BasketOptimiser />

  <h2>What these do not do</h2>
  <p>
    None of these tools reads a live price. Week 9 is where you build the thing
    that does, against a catalogue you chose in week 1, under the crawl-delay
    rules on the <a href={withBase("/policies/")}>policies page</a>. A figure typed into
    this page is a figure you are responsible for.
  </p>
</ContentLayout>

<style is:global>
  .tool {
    margin-block: var(--at-spacing-xl);
    padding: var(--at-spacing-lg);
    border: 1px solid var(--at-border);
    border-radius: var(--at-border-radius);
    background: var(--at-bg-alt);
  }

  .tool > h2 {
    margin-block-start: 0;
  }

  .tool-lede {
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    margin-block-end: var(--at-spacing-lg);
  }

  .tool-body {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--at-spacing-lg);
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }

  @media (min-width: 46rem) {
    .tool-body {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
      align-items: start;
    }
  }

  .tool-fields {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--at-spacing-md);
    margin: 0;
    padding: var(--at-spacing-md);
    border: 1px solid var(--at-divider);
    border-radius: var(--at-border-radius);
    min-inline-size: 0;
  }

  .tool-fields legend {
    padding-inline: var(--at-spacing-xs);
    font-size: var(--at-font-size-sm);
    color: var(--at-text-muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .field {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--at-spacing-xs);
  }

  .field label {
    font-size: var(--at-font-size-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .field input,
  .field select {
    inline-size: 100%;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.6rem;
    font: inherit;
    font-size: var(--at-font-size-sm);
    color: var(--at-text);
    background: var(--at-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--at-border);
    border-radius: var(--at-border-radius);
  }

  .field input[type="range"] {
    padding: 0;
    accent-color: var(--at-primary);
  }

  .field input:focus-visible,
  .field select:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--at-primary);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .field-value {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--at-primary);
  }

  .tool-out {
    display: block;
    min-inline-size: 0;
  }

  .tool-out dl {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--at-spacing-sm);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .tool-out dl > div {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--at-spacing-sm);
    padding-block-end: var(--at-spacing-sm);
    border-block-end: 1px solid var(--at-divider);
  }

  .tool-out dt {
    font-size: var(--at-font-size-sm);
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
  }

  .tool-out dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    color: var(--at-primary);
  }

  /* Wide content scrolls inside its own box rather than the page. */
  .tool-table {
    inline-size: 100%;
    display: block;
    overflow-x: auto;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: var(--at-font-size-sm);
  }

  .tool-table td,
  .tool-table th {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    text-align: start;
  }

  /* At 390px a four-column result table needs every pixel. Tightening it to
     fit beats leaving it to scroll: a clipped table gives no affordance, and
     the numbers either side of the fold are the whole comparison. */
  @media (max-width: 30rem) {
    /* `display: table` with a fixed layout makes the columns share the width
       evenly and wrap inside themselves, so the table fits instead of
       scrolling. Scrolling is the safe default at any width but a poor one
       here: the numbers either side of the fold are the whole comparison, and
       a clipped table offers no hint that there is more. */
    .tool-table {
      display: table;
      table-layout: fixed;
      font-size: 0.78rem;
    }

    .tool-table td,
    .tool-table th {
      padding-inline: 0.25rem;
    }

    /* Numbers must never wrap: "$192.00" broken across two lines reads as
       "$192.0" and a stray zero, which is worse than any amount of clipping. */
    .tool-table td {
      white-space: nowrap;
    }

    /* Prose cells may break; headers get a smaller step so each label stays
       on as few lines as possible. */
    .tool-table th {
      overflow-wrap: break-word;
    }

    /* Four numeric columns do not fit 390px without either breaking a number
       across lines or clipping. Dropping the least load-bearing one — spend,
       which the reader set as an input and which the verdict below restates in
       prose — buys the other three enough room to stay legible. */
    .tool-table .col-spend {
      display: none;
    }

    /* The method names are the longest text here, so give that column the
       slack and split the rest evenly. */
    .tool-table thead th:first-child {
      inline-size: 42%;
    }
  }

  .tool-note,
  .tool-verdict {
    font-size: var(--at-font-size-sm);
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    margin-block: var(--at-spacing-sm) 0;
  }

  .tool-verdict {
    color: var(--at-text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .tool-caution {
    margin-block: var(--at-spacing-lg) 0;
    padding-inline-start: var(--at-spacing-md);
    border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--at-primary);
    font-size: var(--at-font-size-sm);
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
  }

  .visually-hidden {
    position: absolute;
    inline-size: 1px;
    block-size: 1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip-path: inset(50%);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
</style>
